# Vanilla Minecraft Shovel Head - Accurate mesh model
# Based on shovel.json weapon profile
# All coordinates in centimeters
# Shovel oriented PERPENDICULAR to handle
#
# Dimensions from JSON:
# Blade: 120mm (12cm) length, 110mm (11cm) width, 3mm (0.3cm) thickness
# Socket: 60mm (6cm) length, 18mm (1.8cm) outer radius, 14mm (1.4cm) inner radius
# Tip angle: 18 degrees
#
# Coordinate system for perpendicular head:
# - X-axis: along the blade length (primary axis, extends away from handle)
# - Y-axis: handle direction (vertical when attached)
# - Z-axis: blade width direction
# - Origin: at socket/handle junction

# ==============================================================
# SOCKET SECTION (cylindrical tube connecting to handle)
# Socket: 6cm length (Y), 1.8cm outer radius
# Modeled as octagonal prism for efficiency
# ==============================================================

# Socket bottom (Y=0, at handle junction)
# Octagonal outer ring (outer radius 1.8cm)
v 1.27 0.0 1.27
v 1.8 0.0 0.0
v 1.27 0.0 -1.27
v 0.0 0.0 -1.8
v -1.27 0.0 -1.27
v -1.8 0.0 0.0
v -1.27 0.0 1.27
v 0.0 0.0 1.8

# Socket top (Y=6cm, where blade attaches)
v 1.27 6.0 1.27
v 1.8 6.0 0.0
v 1.27 6.0 -1.27
v 0.0 6.0 -1.8
v -1.27 6.0 -1.27
v -1.8 6.0 0.0
v -1.27 6.0 1.27
v 0.0 6.0 1.8

# ==============================================================
# BLADE SECTION (flat paddle shape)
# Blade: 12cm length (X), 11cm width (Z), 0.3cm thickness (simulated as thin)
# Slight dish/curve and tapered tip at 18 degree angle
# ==============================================================

# Blade base (where it meets socket, Y=6cm)
# Full width 11cm (5.5cm each side)
v 1.8 6.0 5.5
v 1.8 5.7 5.5
v 1.8 6.0 -5.5
v 1.8 5.7 -5.5

# Blade at 1/3 length (4cm from socket)
# Maintain full width
v 5.8 6.0 5.5
v 5.8 5.7 5.5
v 5.8 6.0 -5.5
v 5.8 5.7 -5.5

# Blade at 2/3 length (8cm from socket)
# Start tapering width slightly
v 9.8 6.0 5.0
v 9.8 5.7 5.0
v 9.8 6.0 -5.0
v 9.8 5.7 -5.0

# Blade at 5/6 length (10cm from socket)
# Continue taper
v 11.8 6.0 4.0
v 11.8 5.7 4.0
v 11.8 6.0 -4.0
v 11.8 5.7 -4.0

# Blade tip (12cm from socket, Y=6cm)
# Comes to rounded/angled point at 18 degrees
# Tip is still slightly wide (about 2cm) due to rounded tip
v 13.8 6.0 2.0
v 13.8 5.7 2.0
v 13.8 6.0 -2.0
v 13.8 5.7 -2.0

# Very tip (pointed/rounded end)
v 14.5 5.85 0.0

# ==============================================================
# FACES (triangles, CCW winding for outward normals)
# ==============================================================

# ---- SOCKET OUTER SURFACE ----
# Bottom cap of socket (octagon)
f 1 2 3
f 1 3 4
f 1 4 5
f 1 5 6
f 1 6 7
f 1 7 8
f 1 8 2

# Socket side walls (8 rectangles as 16 triangles)
f 1 9 10
f 1 10 2
f 2 10 11
f 2 11 3
f 3 11 12
f 3 12 4
f 4 12 13
f 4 13 5
f 5 13 14
f 5 14 6
f 6 14 15
f 6 15 7
f 7 15 16
f 7 16 8
f 8 16 9
f 8 9 1

# ---- SOCKET TO BLADE TRANSITION ----
# Top surface connections
f 10 17 19
f 10 19 11
f 9 17 10
f 16 9 17

# ---- BLADE TOP SURFACE ----
# Base to 1/3
f 17 21 23
f 17 23 19
# 1/3 to 2/3
f 21 25 27
f 21 27 23
# 2/3 to 5/6
f 25 29 31
f 25 31 27
# 5/6 to tip base
f 29 33 35
f 29 35 31
# Tip triangles
f 33 37 35

# ---- BLADE BOTTOM SURFACE ----
# Base to 1/3
f 18 20 24
f 18 24 22
# 1/3 to 2/3
f 22 24 28
f 22 28 26
# 2/3 to 5/6
f 26 28 32
f 26 32 30
# 5/6 to tip base
f 30 32 36
f 30 36 34
# Tip triangles
f 34 36 37

# ---- BLADE EDGES (right side, +Z) ----
f 17 22 21
f 17 18 22
f 21 26 25
f 21 22 26
f 25 30 29
f 25 26 30
f 29 34 33
f 29 30 34
f 33 34 37

# ---- BLADE EDGES (left side, -Z) ----
f 19 23 24
f 19 24 20
f 23 27 28
f 23 28 24
f 27 31 32
f 27 32 28
f 31 35 36
f 31 36 32
f 35 37 36

# ---- BLADE BACK EDGE (connection to socket) ----
f 17 19 20
f 17 20 18
